00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:38.235
- What is a world champion
boxer, a basketball player,

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:41.542
a track star, or a horse, even animals?

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:45.235
I find out that, this
Mark Spitz, for example,

00:00:45.235 --> 00:00:49.258
he's a world champion, but what made him

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:52.167
the world champion was that he seemed to,

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.864
at the right time, when
the pressure's down, at

00:00:54.864 --> 00:00:58.105
the last few yards, he can get that lead,

00:00:58.105 --> 00:01:00.262
or he's got enough left to make it.

00:01:00.262 --> 00:01:02.609
I fought Ken Norton, my last fight.

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:05.094
The fight was even up
until the last round,

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:07.091
but I had something that he didn't have,

00:01:07.091 --> 00:01:10.505
although I'm much older, that
was the last minute kick.

00:01:10.505 --> 00:01:12.177
- [Interviewer] What's
that last minute kick?

00:01:12.177 --> 00:01:13.097
Is that something?

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:15.181
- It's the stamina, the
strength, the mental capacity

00:01:15.181 --> 00:01:16.664
- [Interviewer] It's more
than training though.

00:01:16.664 --> 00:01:20.019
- to realize what's involved
and how important it is

00:01:20.019 --> 00:01:22.016
to make your body do something
it's really too tired

00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:23.891
to do, your mind makes you do it.

00:01:23.891 --> 00:01:26.572
Mark Spitz, this Olympic
track star was mentioning it.

00:01:26.572 --> 00:01:29.475
He wasn't that much
greater than all the people

00:01:29.475 --> 00:01:32.266
in the world, but sometimes
he won by just that much,

00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:37.201
and a champion is just one
who can come out at the last

00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:38.990
minute and close the show, as they say,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.421
the star closes the show.

00:01:40.421 --> 00:01:43.442
A 14, 15 round fight and
it's even and usually,

00:01:43.442 --> 00:01:46.647
this champion, you can
depend on him to come

00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:48.179
through at the last few seconds,

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:49.859
and find some energy in some words.

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:50.889
- [Interviewer] Is that mental discipline?

00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:51.722
Is it discipline or?

00:01:51.722 --> 00:01:54.296
- Not only that, it's mental and physical.

00:01:54.296 --> 00:01:58.671
His body's in physical shape
to do it, plus, mentally too.

00:01:58.671 --> 00:02:00.979
He's got himself in
condition where both fellas

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:04.398
maybe, sometimes, the
will can outdo the skill,

00:02:04.398 --> 00:02:06.732
and sometimes a fella's
will is stronger than

00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:08.920
the man who's actually better physically

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.159
and the determination
weakens the other man,

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:13.934
just to see him so determined.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.643
- Did you doubt yourself, at any stage?

00:02:16.643 --> 00:02:18.604
Cause it would be
understandable if you did.

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.450
- I never did, no, I
think there was definitely

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.789
times where, not in go-kart,
in go-karts, I was fierce.

00:02:24.789 --> 00:02:26.726
No problems, no whatever.

00:02:26.726 --> 00:02:29.240
Just get out and do what
I do, but I think there

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.841
was a moment when I moved to cars,

00:02:31.841 --> 00:02:33.028
it was really hard.

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:35.059
The first few laps was
going really well and

00:02:35.059 --> 00:02:36.432
then I spun off, I crashed.

00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:38.842
Destroyed the back of the car,

00:02:38.842 --> 00:02:41.080
and I was petrified
because I had to call Ron,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.952
and tell him, and he's not an easy guy to,

00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:46.735
y'know, but he was really supportive.

00:02:46.735 --> 00:02:49.152
He's like "I know that this happens" and

00:02:49.152 --> 00:02:52.353
then we did that first
few races, disaster,

00:02:52.353 --> 00:02:55.852
and there was one day,
there was only one day

00:02:55.852 --> 00:02:57.908
where we got home one day and we sat

00:02:57.908 --> 00:02:59.364
in front of the garage in the car and we

00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:01.304
were talking and it was
like a real down moment.

00:03:01.304 --> 00:03:04.784
Y'know, like, maybe I'm not going
to be able to adapt to this,

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:08.201
from karting to cars, and then I went in,

00:03:10.077 --> 00:03:14.294
had, normal dinner, went to
bed, woke up super early,

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.836
went training, next race, I won.

00:03:16.836 --> 00:03:20.652
Y'know I just, if I ever
had a low moment, the next

00:03:20.652 --> 00:03:22.707
day I just get up with
this determination, I don't

00:03:22.707 --> 00:03:26.131
know where it'd come
from, but I just dug deep,

00:03:26.131 --> 00:03:28.419
and somehow I just managed to find it, so.

00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:30.328
- [Eminem] I was reserved and I was shy,

00:03:30.328 --> 00:03:31.751
and had it in me, but wasn't quite sure

00:03:31.751 --> 00:03:33.269
how to bring it out yet.

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:34.994
I wanted people to hear me so bad,

00:03:34.994 --> 00:03:38.142
and I wanted to do my, but it was like,

00:03:38.142 --> 00:03:41.979
them jitters and then, I'm
scared, I'm not scared.

00:03:41.979 --> 00:03:44.914
That whole struggle and
everything, especially early

00:03:44.914 --> 00:03:47.804
on for me, which I loved being on stage

00:03:47.804 --> 00:03:48.747
and stuff like that.

00:03:48.747 --> 00:03:51.450
Once I got a mic, I was
cool, but it was that,

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.901
it prompted me to do it
and get up there and not

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:58.116
be scared to grab that and just rock.

00:03:58.116 --> 00:04:01.064
I feel like anybody can do
anything they set their mind to.

00:04:01.064 --> 00:04:03.775
It depends on how bad you want
it, and I wanted to do it.

00:04:03.775 --> 00:04:05.718
Y'know, at this stage
in my life I don't feel

00:04:05.718 --> 00:04:07.402
like there's too much that I can't do.

00:04:07.402 --> 00:04:08.929
I don't mean to sound cocky or nothin',

00:04:08.929 --> 00:04:11.094
but if I like really,
really, want to do it,

00:04:11.094 --> 00:04:13.614
I don't give up that easy.

00:04:13.614 --> 00:04:17.552
- When we found out that
cash value life insurance

00:04:17.552 --> 00:04:19.996
was a rip-off and "Buy Term
and Invest the Difference"

00:04:19.996 --> 00:04:22.229
was the way to go, and they
had screwed our family,

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:25.261
I'm tellin' you what, I never forgave them

00:04:25.261 --> 00:04:27.188
for what they did to my mama,

00:04:27.188 --> 00:04:29.214
and what they did to me and Angela,

00:04:29.214 --> 00:04:30.995
and I was out to punish 'em.

00:04:30.995 --> 00:04:32.314
I wanted to hurt 'em,

00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:34.456
and that's the way the
A.L. Williams people were,

00:04:34.456 --> 00:04:37.623
and the more they tried to destroy us,

00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:41.786
the just millions of wars
that we went through,

00:04:41.786 --> 00:04:44.946
you know, when you're a
crusader, crusaders die hard,

00:04:44.946 --> 00:04:47.767
and so it just made us more
determined to show 'em.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:51.068
We wasn't going to let
those, the enemy, defeat us.

00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:54.485
- As an aspiring entrepreneur, I know that

00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:57.902
you've done a lot of things, I don't

00:04:57.902 --> 00:04:59.845
want to go along with your credentials.

00:04:59.845 --> 00:05:00.678
- Thank you.

00:05:00.678 --> 00:05:02.390
- But know that we know that.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:03.469
What do you do?

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:08.099
What did it take for you
to build your empire?

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:12.664
- Man, it took execution,
time after time after time.

00:05:12.664 --> 00:05:14.091
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:05:14.091 --> 00:05:18.258
Proper execution in many
different areas, and consistency.

00:05:21.048 --> 00:05:24.965
It took resilience and
you just have to show up

00:05:26.605 --> 00:05:28.561
and show out, so often.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.521
- [Interviewer] Right on

00:05:29.521 --> 00:05:31.185
- Time after time, you got to wake up,

00:05:31.185 --> 00:05:33.225
and you got to drive, you got to be driven

00:05:33.225 --> 00:05:35.725
to go get somethin' done, now.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.624
I mean, for real, and
it's a gamble sometimes,

00:05:42.624 --> 00:05:45.727
you got to really, really, you
got to be forward thinking,

00:05:45.727 --> 00:05:47.196
ahead of the curve when it comes

00:05:47.196 --> 00:05:49.114
time to make certain decisions.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:53.060
You got to be willing to
stand on your beliefs,

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:56.310
cause a lot of times you're
the only one who can see it.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:57.143
You dig?

00:05:57.143 --> 00:05:58.721
Other people, they don't really see it,

00:05:58.721 --> 00:06:01.507
but you got to really believe
in what you got inside of you

00:06:01.507 --> 00:06:03.173
that's telling you and driving you

00:06:03.173 --> 00:06:04.932
to a certain goal for something.

00:06:04.932 --> 00:06:06.413
- [Interviewer] I can dig.

00:06:06.413 --> 00:06:10.476
- Determination for me is far
more important than desire.

00:06:10.476 --> 00:06:14.446
Desire comes from a place of
thinking "I need it" therefore,

00:06:14.446 --> 00:06:16.971
the presupposition is, "I'm
not good enough, because

00:06:16.971 --> 00:06:18.729
I don't already have it."

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:21.256
Determination is simply
a case of, well, here's

00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:22.809
where I'm focused, here's where I'm going,

00:06:22.809 --> 00:06:26.432
"I don't need it, I'm
just choosing to get it,

00:06:26.432 --> 00:06:29.127
and get out of the damn
way, cause I'm moving."

00:06:29.127 --> 00:06:31.583
- And by the way, there's
always been this kind of thing

00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:33.844
in Silicon Valley of sort
of this, I call it the

00:06:33.844 --> 00:06:34.904
"failure fetish", right?

00:06:34.904 --> 00:06:36.528
Failure is good, right, I can tell

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.312
you guys have all been taught this.

00:06:38.312 --> 00:06:39.768
Heard about this from a lot of people,

00:06:39.768 --> 00:06:40.801
Failure is a wonderful thing,

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.120
failure teaches you all this stuff,

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.501
and it's great to fail a lot,

00:06:43.501 --> 00:06:44.934
and we don't buy any of that.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:47.979
We think that's all
complete, complete nonsense.

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:49.071
We think failure sucks,

00:06:49.071 --> 00:06:50.846
(audience laughter)

00:06:50.846 --> 00:06:52.231
we think failure is

00:06:52.231 --> 00:06:54.956
a terribly, terribly
depressing thing to go through.

00:06:54.956 --> 00:06:57.185
We think, success, on the
other hand, is wonderful.

00:06:57.185 --> 00:06:59.610
You wouldn't think that
this is actually something

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.184
that you have to say out loud, but,

00:07:01.184 --> 00:07:05.451
we do find it to be clarifying,
when we point it out,

00:07:05.451 --> 00:07:07.904
and, so, we are strongly
biased towards people who

00:07:07.904 --> 00:07:10.058
are so determined to
succeed that they just

00:07:10.058 --> 00:07:11.892
never give up, they never quit.

00:07:11.892 --> 00:07:13.535
I think that is a huge part of it,

00:07:13.535 --> 00:07:14.392
and that's something we really look,

00:07:14.392 --> 00:07:16.228
we try to look deeply for.

00:07:16.228 --> 00:07:19.009
That's the kind of thing,
that's not listed on a résumé.

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:20.918
That's something that has
to be deep in somebody's,

00:07:20.918 --> 00:07:22.041
fundamentally deep in
somebody's character,

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:24.067
and you have to see it
in their backgrounds.

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:28.067
- And another important
factor is determination,

00:07:31.733 --> 00:07:35.505
and you should not think
that this development

00:07:35.505 --> 00:07:39.505
can take place within a
few days or a few years.

00:07:41.686 --> 00:07:43.301
We must understand.

00:07:43.301 --> 00:07:46.915
You see that this
development may take eons.

00:07:46.915 --> 00:07:50.595
(audience laughter)

00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:53.632
So you see, our
determination, if you deeply

00:07:53.632 --> 00:07:56.465
consider as a Buddhist and want to

00:07:58.433 --> 00:08:01.484
really practice with the Dharma,

00:08:01.484 --> 00:08:04.528
then, right from the beginning, you must,

00:08:04.528 --> 00:08:07.797
you see, make up your
mind, or it doesn't matter,

00:08:07.797 --> 00:08:11.535
it may take millions of
billions of billions of eons.

00:08:11.535 --> 00:08:13.035
It doesn't matter.

00:08:17.217 --> 00:08:18.268
What's the day?

00:08:18.268 --> 00:08:21.102
After all, what's the purpose of all life?

00:08:21.102 --> 00:08:23.185
The meaning of existence?

00:08:24.184 --> 00:08:27.081
Nothing, utilize something positive,

00:08:27.081 --> 00:08:30.248
then, you see, days or months or eons,

00:08:33.252 --> 00:08:34.669
it is meaningful.

00:08:36.631 --> 00:08:39.899
If you're really wasting your life,

00:08:39.899 --> 00:08:43.649
purpose of life, then
even one day, too long.

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:52.095
So, once you determined,
once you make up your mind,

00:08:52.095 --> 00:08:56.262
some kind of firm determination
and clear objective,

00:08:57.677 --> 00:08:59.927
then time is not important.

00:09:01.153 --> 00:09:05.320
So long as you see, prayer
and so long as pain and

00:09:10.637 --> 00:09:12.645
suffering remains.

00:09:12.645 --> 00:09:16.046
I will remain in order to serve.

00:09:16.046 --> 00:09:20.353
That sentence, really gives
me something to understand,

00:09:20.353 --> 00:09:23.221
and also I think inspiring.

00:09:23.221 --> 00:09:25.692
So the morals is that impatience,

00:09:25.692 --> 00:09:29.101
and as I mentioned before, we want

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:32.044
something done the quickest
or the best or something,

00:09:32.044 --> 00:09:35.301
then I can reserve also,
poorest I think. (laughs)

00:09:35.301 --> 00:09:38.522
The cheapest method,
quickest, cheapest method

00:09:38.522 --> 00:09:42.093
results with the poorest. (laughs)

00:09:42.093 --> 00:09:43.416
That's, I think, wrong.

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.749
So that, I would like to share with you.

00:09:48.269 --> 00:09:51.269
I myself recite some mantra or some

00:09:52.832 --> 00:09:54.999
visualization of mandalas,

00:09:55.919 --> 00:09:58.426
but my daily practice,

00:09:58.426 --> 00:10:01.671
although my practice very poor, very poor,

00:10:01.671 --> 00:10:04.640
but even then, there is a main emphasis

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:08.807
on this Four Noble Truth
and Bodhicitta and Karuna.

00:10:12.334 --> 00:10:15.498
So that really, I feel is
something practical then,

00:10:15.498 --> 00:10:17.350
then through these practices you will

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.017
get something practical benefit.

00:10:20.971 --> 00:10:22.846
Realizations from big deities,

00:10:22.846 --> 00:10:25.513
sometimes I think cheat oneself,

00:10:27.444 --> 00:10:29.882
almost is like cheating oneself.

00:10:29.882 --> 00:10:31.385
- [Interpreter] Deceiving oneself

00:10:31.385 --> 00:10:33.052
- Deceiving oneself!

00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:37.733
So therefore, I think we must practice

00:10:40.028 --> 00:10:44.195
step by step and with patience
and with determination.

00:10:46.359 --> 00:10:50.526
Once you're involved, or
dedicated, or determined,

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:55.744
practice, then some
improvement, you can see.

00:10:55.744 --> 00:10:59.370
You see year-by-year, or
at least decade-by decade.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:03.684
Then you can see or, at least some change,

00:11:03.684 --> 00:11:06.101
some improvement you can see.

00:11:07.021 --> 00:11:10.228
Once you see that, that also gives you,

00:11:10.228 --> 00:11:12.811
some kind of new encouragement.

00:11:14.899 --> 00:11:19.162
So you see, change are not easy, not easy.

00:11:19.162 --> 00:11:21.112
- Hey, when she was little,
and you know, like kids,

00:11:21.112 --> 00:11:22.759
when they're little they're
like "I'm going to be a singer"

00:11:22.759 --> 00:11:24.596
or "I'm going to be an
astronaut", did you ever,

00:11:24.596 --> 00:11:26.724
for one moment, believe
that she would grow to be

00:11:26.724 --> 00:11:28.502
as big as she is right now.

00:11:28.502 --> 00:11:32.676
- Actually, as a child, she was
very childish to begin with.

00:11:32.676 --> 00:11:35.375
As a child. (laughter)

00:11:35.375 --> 00:11:38.475
- [Host] A very childish child actually.

00:11:38.475 --> 00:11:41.823
- She was very determined, alright,

00:11:41.823 --> 00:11:45.551
and we could see it, when she was four.

00:11:45.551 --> 00:11:46.622
- I'm so embarrassed.

00:11:46.622 --> 00:11:48.800
- You know, she would
stand in front of the piano

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.808
and just bang on the keys,

00:11:50.808 --> 00:11:54.309
and then she wrote her first song,

00:11:54.309 --> 00:11:57.280
it was, I used to play
"Money" by Pink Floyd,

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:01.566
and she wrote her first song,
it was called "Dollar Bill."

00:12:01.566 --> 00:12:02.607
- [Host] I love that.

00:12:02.607 --> 00:12:04.963
- And, Cynthia, my wife, she still has it.

00:12:04.963 --> 00:12:06.369
- [Host] We should have that.

00:12:06.369 --> 00:12:09.036
- You know it's because
you know, on that record,

00:12:09.036 --> 00:12:13.203
they use actual money and
the register as instruments,

00:12:14.995 --> 00:12:17.892
and I remember as a kid I
was so fascinated by that,

00:12:17.892 --> 00:12:20.446
so my dad played me a
lot of great music that

00:12:20.446 --> 00:12:23.993
made me really fall in love
with the idea of making it.

00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:26.994
- The very minute that
you decide upon something,

00:12:26.994 --> 00:12:28.663
you know that's what you want, you know

00:12:28.663 --> 00:12:30.343
you're going to do it,

00:12:30.343 --> 00:12:33.014
all of these negative that
have been bothering you,

00:12:33.014 --> 00:12:36.264
they pick up their baggage and get out.

